    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119784,
      "id": "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54",
      "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 3, column 1 is $7\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is diagonal: **false**. The entry in row 3, column 1 is $7\\ne 0$, off the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "b320899c-ecc5-591b-94dc-af39c9ac7f63",
